    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768">

                <pb facs="1043" n="1029" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1029"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.9321/8–2444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-05T18:00:00-04:00">September 5,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1173. 1. Department authorizes insertion of words “without delay” in last
                    sentence, paragraph 2, Article VIII draft Consular Convention (your 1453, August
                    24, 4 p.m.).</p>
                <p>2. With a view to meeting points raised in second paragraph of reference
                    telegram, please reword first sentence of paragraph 2, Article VII to read as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The quarters where consular business is conducted, all consular
                            correspondence in transit under official seal and all papers, records
                            and correspondence comprising the consular archives shall at all times
                            be inviolable, and under no pretext shall any authorities of any
                            character of the country in which such quarters or archives are located
                            invade such premises or make any examination or seizure of papers or
                            other property in such quarters or of such archives.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>3. Department suggests that you defer presentation of Consular Convention to
                    Foreign Office in order that you may make such further comments as you may
                    desire.</p>
                <p>4. When draft is presented to Chinese Foreign Office you may at such time give a
                    copy confidentially to your British colleague. Please inform Department of exact
                    date you propose to present draft to the Chinese.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
